my-id "q-128490" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\n- $det(M)=10$\n- $det(M)=-5$\n- $M$ is a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1912b5b-58a0-5491-a50c-b728a4ed3e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059299} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f7c0b0-c3a5-549e-b078-15d79f0248eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059300} {:answer/id #uuid "06c85cfe-b123-504b-9faf-324c33d747ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 1759